{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createThrottledValue<TValue, TSelected>(\n   host,\n   source,\n   options,\n   selector?): [CellValue<TValue>, LitThrottler<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/lit-pacer/src/throttler/createThrottledValue.ts#L37","children":[{"type":"text","value":"throttler/createThrottledValue.ts:37"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derives a throttled value from its current source."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits execution to the configured wait interval. Leading and trailing execution are enabled by default, and the latest blocked update is retained for the trailing edge."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"return-value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns [value, utility]. The value is an accessor; call value() from render(). Pass a getter that reads reactive source state. The initial value is available immediately. Source changes schedule updates on the existing utility."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-and-ownership","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State and ownership"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the owning ReactiveControllerHost first. Host updates refresh options. Disconnecting runs cleanup; reconnecting restores subscriptions to the same utility.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"host","children":[{"type":"text","value":"host"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactiveControllerHost"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"source","children":[{"type":"text","value":"source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ValueSource"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/LitPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/LitThrottlerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitThrottlerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SetValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CellValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/LitThrottler.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitThrottler"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SetValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createThrottledValue } from '@tanstack/lit-pacer'\n\n// In a LitElement constructor:\n// query is a reactive property on this host.\nconst [value, utility] = createThrottledValue(this, () => this.query, { wait: 500 })\n// Bind value and use utility for controls. Read value() for the committed value.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createThrottler"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"return-value","text":"Return value","level":2},{"id":"state-and-ownership","text":"State and ownership","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"host","text":"host","level":3},{"id":"source","text":"source","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createThrottledValue<TValue, TSelected>(\n   host,\n   source,\n   options,\n   selector?): [CellValue<TValue>, LitThrottler<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [throttler/createThrottledValue.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/lit-pacer/src/throttler/createThrottledValue.ts#L37)\n\nDerives a throttled value from its current source.\n\nLimits execution to the configured wait interval. Leading and trailing execution are enabled by default, and the latest blocked update is retained for the trailing edge.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns [value, utility]. The value is an accessor; call value() from render(). Pass a getter that reads reactive source state. The initial value is available immediately. Source changes schedule updates on the existing utility.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nThe value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them.\n\nPass the owning ReactiveControllerHost first. Host updates refresh options. Disconnecting runs cleanup; reconnecting restores subscriptions to the same utility.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### host\n\n`ReactiveControllerHost`\n\n### source\n\n`ValueSource`\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`LitPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/LitPacerOptions.md)\\<[`LitThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/LitThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`CellValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, [`LitThrottler`](../interfaces/LitThrottler.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { createThrottledValue } from '@tanstack/lit-pacer'\n\n// In a LitElement constructor:\n// query is a reactive property on this host.\nconst [value, utility] = createThrottledValue(this, () => this.query, { wait: 500 })\n// Bind value and use utility for controls. Read value() for the committed value.\n```\n\n## See\n\ncreateThrottler\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createThrottledValue\ntitle: createThrottledValue\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createThrottledValue<TValue, TSelected>(\n   host,\n   source,\n   options,\n   selector?): [CellValue<TValue>, LitThrottler<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [throttler/createThrottledValue.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/lit-pacer/src/throttler/createThrottledValue.ts#L37)\n\nDerives a throttled value from its current source.\n\nLimits execution to the configured wait interval. Leading and trailing execution are enabled by default, and the latest blocked update is retained for the trailing edge.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns [value, utility]. The value is an accessor; call value() from render(). Pass a getter that reads reactive source state. The initial value is available immediately. Source changes schedule updates on the existing utility.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nThe value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them.\n\nPass the owning ReactiveControllerHost first. Host updates refresh options. Disconnecting runs cleanup; reconnecting restores subscriptions to the same utility.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### host\n\n`ReactiveControllerHost`\n\n### source\n\n`ValueSource`\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`LitPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/LitPacerOptions.md)\\<[`LitThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/LitThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`CellValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, [`LitThrottler`](../interfaces/LitThrottler.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { createThrottledValue } from '@tanstack/lit-pacer'\n\n// In a LitElement constructor:\n// query is a reactive property on this host.\nconst [value, utility] = createThrottledValue(this, () => this.query, { wait: 500 })\n// Bind value and use utility for controls. Read value() for the committed value.\n```\n\n## See\n\ncreateThrottler\n"}
